[OPTIONS]
.Version = 6
.DEoption = 20
.Integer Levels = 8
.Integer Shape = 0
.Double Size = 1
.Double CSize X = 0.92436
.Double CSize Y = 0.90756
.Double CSize Z = 0.92436
.Double Julia X = 0
.Double Julia Y = 0
.Double Julia Z = 0
.Double Thickness = 0.01
.Double DE offset = 0
.Double Offset X = 0
.Double Offset Y = 0
.Double Offset Z = 0
.Double Colour scale = 2
[CODE]
C746E000000000C746E4FFFFEF7FB86D623364B82D727320B850736575B8646F4B
6CB865696E00C3
[END]

Knighty's Pseudo Kleinian (Theli-at's pseudo Kleinian hybrid as one
formula, Fragmentarium 2011): each level folds the point into the box
CSize (2*clamp(p) - p), inverts it in the sphere of radius sqrt(Size)
when it is inside (p *= max(Size/r2, 1)), and adds Julia. The distance
is that of the folded point to a shape, divided by the accumulated
scale: Shape 0 the floor plane z = Offset Z (the classic look), 1 a
cylinder-plane of Thickness through Offset, 2 a rounded unit box
(rounded by Thickness) at Offset. DE offset hollows the surface.

Calculated by mb3d-rs itself (the code above is only a placeholder; the
original Mandelbulb3D shows nothing with this formula).

The colour value (orbit trap, "2nd choice" in the Lighting) is the
smallest distance of the folded point from the origin over the levels,
scaled by Colour scale. Use 1 iteration; the structure fills space, so
look at it from inside (knighty: CSize 0.92436, 0.90756, 0.92436).
